- [ ] Profile cold and warm swipes, including a long fling and several settled album changes, on the same phone and library. Record time from card visibility to artwork and from settle to artwork-led colors, plus janky frame rate and P95 frame time. Use `adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo com.evanna.player reset` and `adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo com.evanna.player framestats`. Use Perfetto to distinguish decode, Compose, and rendering. Repeat three runs per case.
- [ ] In `library/CarouselScreen.kt`, let the settled album's tracks and summary publish independently of artwork and accent. The current selection waits for both database results and cover/accent work. Reuse `EmbeddedArtwork.album(album, ArtworkSize.MEDIUM)` and share the result within Carousel by album identity and artwork revision. Use bounded preloading for the center and immediate neighbors via the existing pager window. Publish the cover and accent as they become ready. Protect against canceled work applying an old album or revision. Ensure artwork-only updates do not reset the track list or pagination.
- [ ] Reuse `CarouselBackdrops` and `sampleArtworkAccent`. Keep expensive preparation off the UI thread, prioritize the settled album's backdrop, and retain the preceding theme until the new artwork result is known. Ease to the default theme when the settled album has no cover. Review `CarouselAlbumCard` blur and the artwork backdrop in the trace. If rendering is a bottleneck, keep the center sharp and reduce per-frame side-cover blur changes, preserving the visual hierarchy.
- [ ] Re-run the baseline and record before/after medians. Verify improved cold artwork/theme latency and smoother flings within run-to-run variance. Check rapid reversals, missing and replaced art, matching title/different artist, no stale colors, smooth light/dark transitions, and stable track scrolling while artwork arrives.

## 5. Mini-player to Now Playing

- [ ] In `PlayerSheet.kt`, keep `FlyingCover` and its bounds interpolation. The full-screen chrome currently moves with `graphicsLayer { translationY = motion.offsetY }` while the cover uses separate coordinates. For tap/open and programmatic close, keep the chrome at its final coordinates and use the progress-driven backdrop and controls alpha already in `NowPlaying.kt`. Retain the vertical offset during direct drags and their settling animation. Carry the drag/programmatic mode through settling so releasing a partial drag does not jump.
